---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../lib/config';
import { useTranslation, getLocaleFromUrl, getLocalizedPath } from '../i18n/utils';
import type { Locale } from '../i18n/languages';

interface Props {
  locale?: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
const currentLocale = locale || getLocaleFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslation(currentLocale);
const contactUrl = getLocalizedPath('/contact/', currentLocale);
const termsUrl = getLocalizedPath('/terms-of-service/', currentLocale);
---

<ContentLayout
  title={t.pages.disclaimer.title}
  description={t.pages.disclaimer.description}
  locale={currentLocale}
  keywords="disclaimer, disposable email terms, temporary email usage disclaimer, anonymous temp mail notice"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 21, 2026
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>TempoEmails</strong> (at <strong>{SITE_CONFIG.domain}</strong>) and the information on this site are provided "as is" and "as available", for convenience, privacy and software testing only.
  </p>

  <p>
    By using TempoEmails you accept the limitations described below.
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <strong>Important:</strong> TempoEmails inboxes are temporary, and many of them have no password. <strong>Never</strong> use a temporary address for banking, financial accounts, account recovery, medical records or confidential mail.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>1. Nature of the Disposable Email Service</h2>
  <p>
    TempoEmails is a receive-only interface for short-lived inboxes hosted by third-party providers (Mail.tm, Mail.gw, Inboxes, TempMail.lol and Guerrilla Mail). You understand that:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Many inboxes are public:</strong> Inboxes, Guerrilla Mail and TempMail.lol addresses have no password. Anyone who knows or guesses the address can read its mail. Mail.tm and Mail.gw inboxes have a generated password, but anyone who has it can open the inbox.</li>
    <li><strong>Limited recovery:</strong> a Mail.tm or Mail.gw inbox can be reopened with its password while the provider still has it. Other inboxes can't be recovered, and neither we nor the providers can restore messages that have been deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Receive-only:</strong> you can't send or reply from a TempoEmails address.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. No Guarantee of Message Delivery or Permanence</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We can't guarantee that any particular email will be received or displayed.</strong> Delivery depends on things outside our control:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Blocked domains:</strong> some websites detect and block disposable email domains and won't send to them.</li>
    <li><strong>Sender and network problems:</strong> the sender's mail server may delay, reject or drop a message before it reaches the provider.</li>
    <li><strong>Provider changes:</strong> providers can change or retire their domains, go offline, or shut down without warning.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> each provider deletes inboxes and messages on its own schedule. TempMail.lol inboxes, for example, expire after about an hour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Not for Sensitive or Critical Communications</h2>
  <p>
    TempoEmails is meant for low-risk, short-term uses such as one-time confirmation links, testing signups, or getting past an email gate. <strong>Don't use it for:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Banking, credit union, or financial service accounts.</li>
    <li>Cryptocurrency exchange registrations, wallet recoveries, or two-factor seed verifications.</li>
    <li>Government portals, tax documentation, legal filings, or official notices.</li>
    <li>Your main social media, work or long-term accounts.</li>
    <li>Receiving personal information, medical records or business secrets.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    TempoEmails isn't liable for locked accounts, lost funds, compromised credentials or missed messages that result from using a temporary address for something important.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-Party Links & Received Email Content</h2>
  <p>
    Emails shown in TempoEmails come from third parties. We remove scripts and tracking pixels before displaying them, but we don't check or endorse what they say:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Links and attachments:</strong> messages may contain phishing links, harmful attachments or misleading claims. Opening them is at your own risk.</li>
    <li><strong>Other websites:</strong> links in emails or on our site may lead to websites we don't run. We aren't responsible for their content or practices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Advertising & Endorsements</h2>
  <p>
    If you accept cookies, TempoEmails shows ads from Google AdSense. Showing an ad doesn't mean we endorse or recommend the product, service or company advertised.
  </p>
  <p>
    We aren't responsible for any dealings between you and an advertiser.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Reliance on Mail Providers</h2>
  <p>
    TempoEmails doesn't operate mail servers; it relies on the providers named above and their public APIs. If the preferred provider is unavailable, TempoEmails tries the others, but all of them can be slow or down at the same time. When none can be reached, the site shows a clearly labelled simulated inbox that can't receive real mail. We aren't liable for losses caused by provider outages, changes or errors.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Modifications to This Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Disclaimer at any time. Changes take effect when posted here, and the date at the top shows the latest version.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Disclaimer:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONFIG.emails.contact}`}>{SITE_CONFIG.emails.contact}</a></li>
    <li><strong>Contact Page:</strong> <a href={contactUrl}>TempoEmails Support Desk</a></li>
    <li><strong>Terms of Service:</strong> <a href={termsUrl}>View Terms of Service</a></li>
  </ul>
</ContentLayout>
